  ▎ nexus  claude

    I fixed `peek()`, and `node test.js` now prints `OK`.
    
    The bug was an off-by-one error. `peek()` read `this.items[this.items.length]`, which is one slot past the end of the array, so it always got `undefined`. It now reads `this.items[this.items.length - 1]` (`stack.js:5`), which is the most recently pushed item, and it doesn't remove anything from the stack.
    
    On an empty stack, `peek()` returns `undefined`, while `pop()` throws an error. The tests don't check this case. If you want `peek()` to throw too, I can make that change.
    


